module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_unreached_measurement_renders_as_a_failed_one

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_unreached_measurement_renders_as_a_failed_one: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_unreached_measurement_renders_as_a_failed_one" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an unreached measurement renders as a failed one** (a required lane that never reached its subject -- the instrument would not build, the runner died, the checkout refused -- reports at the decision surface identically to a lane that reached its subject and refused it. Both are one red. One carries a verdict about every identity it adjudicated; the other carries a verdict about NOTHING, and the surface does not say which it is.",

    "INVALID STATE: a red that is read as evidence about its declared subject when the subject was never evaluated. The record is not false -- the job did fail -- but `failed` at the presentation boundary is a coproduct collapsed to one variant, and the discarded variant is the one that says the measurement does not exist.",

    "HARM, AND IT IS MISDIRECTED WORK RATHER THAN AN ADMITTED BREAK, which is what separates it from required_evidence_absent_reads_as_evidence_of_pass. That class fails OPEN: a gate admits because nothing reported. This one fails toward WASTE: nothing is admitted, but every reader attributes the red to the subject named on the lane. Lanes debug witnesses that never ran. A landed repair is read as having failed when its own run never adjudicated an identity, so the repair gets reverted or re-attempted while the real defect -- infrastructure -- stays invisible precisely because its symptom is indistinguishable from ordinary red. The two classes are opposite directions out of the same missing distinction.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the first is mechanical enough to apply without reading the log. The adjudication STANDING already names the difference: standing=measurement_unreached with cause=instrument could not be built, against standing=measurement_completed blockers=N. Second, VOLUME: an unreached lane emits no per-identity adjudication at all, so its log carries ZERO `identity=` lines, while a completed-with-blockers lane carries one per blocker. On the specimen below that is ~86-88 KB with zero against ~1.19 MB with eleven. Either test separates them in one grep; the surface that decides merges applies neither.",

    "SPECIMEN (2026-09-11, gunbc main). Two consecutive main runs on two slots of one host reported required-witnesses-floor FAILURE with standing=measurement_unreached: srv4-04 on run 34570523344 (head d94bcf680) could not read a cargo registry source file mid-compile, and srv4-16 on run 34571176215 (head ec1571e89) could not write a target .rmeta. Both are ENOENT rather than ENOSPC, which is what rules out a full disk and is itself a distinguishing fact worth keeping. THE COST LANDED EXACTLY WHERE THIS CLASS PREDICTS: d94bcf680 IS #11032, the repair for a separate witness-budget defect that had main red, so the one run that could have told its lane whether the repair worked reported red while measuring nothing -- and the natural reading, `still red after the fix`, was unsupported in either direction. Three lanes were downstream of that misreading.",

    "NOT THE SAME AS A FLAKE, and the distinction matters for what to do next: a flake is a measurement that reached its subject and got the wrong answer, so re-running samples the same distribution. An unreached measurement has no answer to sample; re-running is only worth doing if the reason it could not reach is itself transient, and NOTHING IN THE RED SAYS WHETHER IT IS. Treating the two alike is how a broken runner gets re-run indefinitely.",

    "RUNG: found at 1, mitigatable. The distinction is not lost -- the standing field is typed and present in the log, so a reader who opens it can always recover which case they are in. What is lost is that the DECIDING surface does not carry it, so recovery depends on a human knowing to look, which is exactly the dependency a mitigation has and a guarantee does not.",

    "CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed, and reachable without new language capability. The lane already computes the standing; the check conclusion is simply not derived from it. A conclusion derived from the adjudication standing rather than from the job's exit code makes an unreached measurement a distinct reported state by construction, and no reader can conflate two states the surface renders differently. It is not 4: the underlying event -- a runner losing its filesystem -- remains external reality and cannot be given no constructor.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability rather than an artifact: a required-lane conclusion derived from the adjudication standing, SUFFICIENT FOR an unreached measurement to present at the merge surface as its own state rather than as a failure. Emitting the standing into the log is not the trigger -- it is already there, and this row exists because that was not enough. The trigger is the surface consuming it.",

    "REVIEW TELL: anyone attributing a red to a named witness, lane, or change without having seen an adjudicated identity for it. Ask for the identity line. If the log has none, the red is about the instrument and the subject has not been measured -- and any statement about that subject, in either direction, is unsupported.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
